<svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-arogya-title" tabindex="-1">Arogya</h3><p class="record__kicker">Healthcare · Hackathon build · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A healthcare RAG prototype that checks access, evidence, and citations before producing an answer.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>Python</li><li>FastAPI</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>React</li><li>Vite</li><li>BM25</li><li>Sentence Transformers</li><li>Docker</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/Arogya" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/arogya/arogya.mp4" aria-label="Arogya walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><h4>Problem</h4><p>In healthcare information retrieval, a confident answer can still be unsafe if its evidence is missing or inaccessible to the reader.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>Arogya retrieves from a synthetic hospital knowledge base. The pipeline applies role checks, combines lexical and semantic retrieval, considers conflicting or superseded documents, and refuses when evidence is insufficient. Its interface exposes citations and evaluation views. The repository uses synthetic records and is not intended for clinical use.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Role-aware retrieval</li><li>Document lifecycle and conflict handling</li><li>Evidence sufficiency and refusal</li><li>Sentence-level citation checks</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>React interface → FastAPI pipeline → permission-filtered PostgreSQL evidence → hybrid retrieval and reranking → local generation and citation checks.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-genshakti" data-record-view="genshakti" hidden aria-labelledby="record-genshakti-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-genshakti-title" tabindex="-1">GenShakti</h3><p class="record__kicker">AI &amp; Data · Group project · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A renewable-energy planning prototype combining maps, site-selection interfaces, and AI-generated guidance.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>React</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>Vite</li><li>Leaflet</li><li>React Flow</li><li>Hugging Face</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://genshakti.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 1