gy savings or validated site rankings.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Map-based site exploration</li><li>Energy-planning guidance</li><li>Flow and chart interfaces</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>React/Vite browser interface combines map/flow components with external model-service integration.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-xeno-crm" data-record-view="xeno-crm" hidden aria-labelledby="record-xeno-crm-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-xeno-crm-title" tabindex="-1">XenoCRM Mini</h3><p class="record__kicker">Full-stack · Assignment · Prototype</p><p class="lead">An engineering-assignment CRM prototype for customer segments, campaign workflows, and AI-assisted planning.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>React</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Node.js</li><li>Express</li><li>Prisma</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>Groq</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://xeno-crm-frontend-tan.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/xeno-crm-backend" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/xeno-crm/xenocrm.mp4" aria-label="XenoCRM Mini walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><h4>Problem</h4><p>Marketing workflows need customer data, audience rules, campaign actions, and delivery feedback to fit together.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>The React frontend talks to an Express API backed by Prisma and PostgreSQL. Groq supports AI-assisted campaign interactions. A separate channel stub generates delivery callbacks, allowing campaign state transitions to be demonstrated without claiming real message delivery.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Customer and segment management</li><li>Campaign creation</li><li>AI-assisted campaign interaction</li><li>Simulated delivery callbacks</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>React/TypeScript client → Express API → Prisma/PostgreSQL; Groq integration and a separate delivery stub with asynchronous callbacks.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-vigil-ai" data-record-view="vigil-ai" hidden aria-labelledby="record-vigil-ai-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-vigil-ai-title" tabindex="-1">VigilAI</h3><p class="record__kicker">AI &amp; Data · Assignment · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A retail-analytics challenge project connecting video events to a store-intelligence dashboard.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>Python</li><li>OpenCV</li><li>YOLO</li><li>FastAPI</li><li>SQLite</li><li>Redis</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>Docker</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://vigilai-nu.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/vigilai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/vigil-ai/vigilai.mp4" poster="/review-media/review/derived/vigil-ai/weboutput.1280.webp" aria-label="VigilAI walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><ul class="gallery" role="list" aria-label="Screenshots"><li><a href="/review-media/review/derived/vigil-ai/weboutput.1280.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View larger image: VigilAI — interface capture (opens in a new tab)"><img src="/review-media/review/derived/vigil-ai/weboutput.480.webp" width="480" height="242" alt="VigilAI — interface capture" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a></li></ul><h4>Problem</h4><p>Store activity is difficult to interpret when detection events, zones, and business views remain disconnected.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>VigilAI includes a YOLO-based detection pipeline, visitor tracking, zone mapping, event ingestion, and a FastAPI analytics service. A browser dashboard presents funnels, dwell-time views, heatmaps, and anomalies. The project is presented as a challenge prototype; footage rights, identification risks, and metric validity require separate review.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Video-event pipeline</li><li>Zone and visitor-event processing</li><li>Analytics API</li><li>Funnel and heatmap dashboard</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>Video detection/tracking and zone mapping → event ingestion → FastAPI/SQLite analytics, with Redis-supported event transport and a browser dashboard.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-devstudy" data-record-view="devstudy" hidden aria-labelledby="record-devstudy-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-devstudy-title" tabindex="-1">DevStudy</h3><p class="record__kicker">Tools · Experiment · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A developer-learning prototype with code editors, browser previews, and a diagramming workspace.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>Next.js</li><li>React</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Monaco Editor</li><li>Mermaid</li><li>Socket.IO</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://devstudy-ten.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/Devstudy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/devstudy/edtech.mp4" aria-label="DevStudy walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough — part of a combined BuildLog episode; it starts at this project’s segment. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><h4>Problem</h4><p>Learning software development often means moving between code exercises and architecture diagrams.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>DevStudy combines a Monaco-based editor, web previews, and a Mermaid diagram workspace. The repository describes local execution for web languages and remote execution through Piston for other languages, with a Socket.IO service for battle interactions. Availability of external execution and collaboration services has not been functionally tested.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Code-editor workspace</li><li>HTML/CSS preview</li><li>Mermaid diagram editor</li><li>Remote execution integration</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>Next.js UI combines Monaco and Mermaid workspaces; Piston handles remote-language execution and a separate Socket.IO server supports battle flows.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-aadhaar-pulse" data-record-view="aadhaar-pulse" hidden aria-labelledby="record-aadhaar-pulse-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-aadhaar-pulse-title" tabindex="-1">AadhaarPulse</h3><p class="record__kicker">AI &amp; Data · Hackathon build · Prototype</p><p class="lead">An analytics prototype for exploring district-level Aadhaar authentication patterns and service demand.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>Next.js</li><li>React</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Python</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li><li>Recharts</li><li>Leaflet</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://aadhaar-pulse.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5