ent. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><h4>Problem</h4><p>Exploring a document often requires both reading its pages and asking focused questions about its text.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>QueryPDF combines PDF.js with a Transformers.js model and a document-viewing interface. The design keeps document processing in the browser after the required assets load. It should be described as a prototype; first-load downloads and browser resource requirements need testing on the target device.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>PDF viewer</li><li>Document questions</li><li>Summary and quiz interfaces</li><li>Browser-side model integration</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>Browser PDF.js extraction and viewer → client-side Transformers.js model → question, summary and quiz interfaces.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-sentinel-agent" data-record-view="sentinel-agent" hidden aria-labelledby="record-sentinel-agent-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-sentinel-agent-title" tabindex="-1">Sentinel Agent</h3><p class="record__kicker">Web3 · Experiment · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A scripted smart-contract security demonstration with exploit tests, a patch flow, and streamed progress.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>React</li><li>Node.js</li><li>Express</li><li>Solidity</li><li>Hardhat</li><li>Ethers.js</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://sentinel-agent-lovat.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/Sentinel-Agent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/sentinel-agent/sentinel-agent.mp4" poster="/review-media/review/derived/sentinel-agent/screenshort.1280.webp" aria-label="Sentinel Agent walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><ul class="gallery" role="list" aria-label="Screenshots"><li><a href="/review-media/review/derived/sentinel-agent/screenshort.1280.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View larger image: Sentinel Agent — interface capture (opens in a new tab)"><img src="/review-media/review/derived/sentinel-agent/screenshort.480.webp" width="480" height="243" alt="Sentinel Agent — interface capture" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a></li></ul><h4>Problem</h4><p>Explaining a contract vulnerability is more useful when the exploit and corrective change can be followed.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>The server streams a predefined audit sequence, runs Hardhat tests around a reentrancy example, and replaces the example contract with a checks-effects-interactions version. The reasoning messages and model behaviour are simulated. This demonstrates a workflow, without claiming a general autonomous auditor.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Reentrancy example</li><li>Hardhat test integration</li><li>Scripted patch and re-test flow</li><li>Server-sent progress events</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>React dashboard consumes Express SSE events; the server runs a scripted contract/test/patch sequence through Hardhat.</p><p class="flag" data-review-mode>Needs owner review · media not yet cleared for release.</p></article><article class="record" id="record-shayoga" data-record-view="shayoga" hidden aria-labelledby="record-shayoga-title"><a class="back" href="/projects/" data-nav="projects"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20.5 12h-16M10 6.5 4.5 12l5.5 5.5"/></svg> Projects</a><h3 class="record__title" id="record-shayoga-title" tabindex="-1">Shayoga</h3><p class="record__kicker">Web3 · Experiment · Prototype</p><p class="lead">A Web3 crowdfunding prototype with campaign browsing, wallet connection, and donation-contract flows.</p><ul class="tags" role="list" aria-label="Technologies"><li>React</li><li>Vite</li><li>Solidity</li><li>Hardhat</li><li>Ethers.js</li><li>Tailwind CSS</li></ul><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://shayoga.netlify.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></s