cel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open demo <svg class="icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13.5 4h6.5v6.5M20 4l-9 9M17.5 14v5.5h-13v-13H10"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/URAYUSHJAIN/Slotly" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 19.6c-4 1.2-4-2-5.6-2.4M14.6 21.6v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.6-1.4 5.6-6.2a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1.3-3.3 4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1-3.3s-1-.3-3.4 1.3a11.6 11.6 0 0 0-6 0C6.5 3.1 5.4 3.4 5.4 3.4a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-.1 3.3A4.8 4.8 0 0 0 4 10c0 4.8 2.8 5.9 5.6 6.2-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2v3.4"/></svg> View source on GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div><figure class="media"><video controls preload="none" playsinline src="/review-media/review/projects/slotly/slotly.mp4" aria-label="Slotly walkthrough video"></video><figcaption>Project walkthrough. No captions are available; the description below covers the same work.</figcaption></figure><h4>Problem</h4><p>Booking interfaces need to connect a patient’s selected time with a doctor’s availability.</p><h4>What it does</h4><p>Slotly uses a React frontend and Neon/PostgreSQL services for account and scheduling flows. The repository contains role-specific screens and booking components. It is an assessment project, without claiming employment at the assessment organization or a deployed clinical service.</p><h4>Verified features</h4><ul class="bullets"><li>Patient and doctor interfaces</li><li>Availability management</li><li>Appointment-booking flow</li></ul><h4>Architecture</h4><p>React/Vite role-specific interfaces → Neon authentication/data ser